/**
 * R7 BLOCK #1 layer (b): SlackInstructionProvider must NOT leak another tenant's
 * Slack identity. Its connection reads are agent-/id-scoped and — without an
 * ambient org — would return ANOTHER org's Slack connection for a shared agent
 * id (foreign botUsername/botUserId). So:
 *   - orgless context ⇒ no identity is read or rendered;
 *   - org-present ⇒ the read runs INSIDE the token org (orgContext.run).
 *
 * The generic participant framing is org-independent and carries no tenant
 * data, so it is still emitted when orgless — only the IDENTITY is withheld.
 */

