424	  // conversation a run came from when several are possible (a Slack channel, a
425	  // Telegram thread); on `api` there is only ever the chat the user is looking
426	  // at, so "Platform: api" / "Channel: api_<userId>" is pure noise. It is also
427	  // the one surface where the block is visibly harmful: pi records whatever
428	  // string is handed to `session.prompt()` into the transcript, so the injected
429	  // scaffolding replays into the UI attributed to the user. Suppressing it at
430	  // the source keeps the web transcript equal to what the user actually typed —
