13	 * usually-non-deterministic miss (the model "forgot" the closing step). A
14	 * bounded re-dispatch gives it a fresh turn to finalize. Default 1 (one extra
15	 * attempt); 0 disables. Each re-dispatch is a full agent turn, so keep it low.
16	 *
17	 * NOTE: this is a re-dispatch (a fresh session via the existing dispatch loop),
18	 * not a warm in-session nudge — the agent-worker is platform-agnostic and has
19	 * no notion of watchers/complete_window, so a worker-side self-nudge would
20	 * break that isolation. This constant is the GLOBAL default; a watcher can
21	 * override it via execution_config.finalize_nudges (see
22	 * resolveFinalizeNudgeBudget). A declarative defineBehavior surface for it is
23	 * the remaining follow-up (the CLI doesn't expose execution_config yet).
