10	 * NOT in `findMatchingBehaviorActivations`. The lookup is an unlocked SELECT,
11	 * so two concurrent deliveries would both read "no recent activation" and both
12	 * fire. `debounces two concurrent deliveries` below is the regression test for
13	 * that; it fails against a cooldown evaluated during the match.
14	 *
15	 * WHY ONLY THE EVENT PATH: a schedule already spaces its own firings — cron IS
16	 * the operator's cadence control — so a cooldown there is redundant. Worse, the
17	 * scheduled path would have to skip materializing a run, and `next_run_at` only
18	 * advances when a run reaches a terminal state (see `advanceWatcherSchedule`).
19	 * A suppressed scheduled firing would leave the cursor in the past and the
